+# CVE-2026-73089 — False Positive Assessment for browserslist@3.2.8
+
+## Summary
+
+**CVE-2026-73089 does not affect browserslist 3.2.8.**
+The unbounded query-result `cache` / `parseCache` objects in `index.js` were introduced in 4.7.2. This version has no such cache. There is nothing to patch.
+
+---
+
+## CVE Description
+
+Prior to 4.28.7, `index.js` retains every distinct `(queries, context)` result in `cache` and every `parseQueries()` AST in `parseCache` without a size cap, TTL, or eviction. An attacker who can influence repeated `browserslist()` query values can cause linear memory growth and an out-of-memory crash.
+
+- **CVE ID:** CVE-2026-73089
+- **GHSA:** GHSA-c83g-rgw3-j3cx
+- **CWE:** CWE-770
+- **Severity:** High (CVSS 7.5)
+- **Upstream fix commit:** `f2931a3ff2a3a31abf84ef01a7400b270aad6405` — Fix unbounded memory growth
+- **Fixed version:** 4.28.7
+
+---
+
+## Affected Package
+
+| Field | Value |
+|---|---|
+| Ecosystem | npm |
+| Package | browserslist |
+| This version | 3.2.8 |
+| Scanner range | < 4.28.7 (introduced: 0) |
+
+---
+
+## Root Cause of the CVE
+
+```js
+var cache = {}
+var parseCache = {}
+// ...
+if (cache[cacheKey]) return cache[cacheKey]
+cache[cacheKey] = result
+```
+
+The GHSA is explicit that this is **not** `node.js`'s `filenessCache` / `configCache` (filesystem caches). Those are a different subsystem.
+
+---
+
+## Why 3.2.8 Is Not Affected
+
+### 1. The vulnerable cache was introduced after 3.2.8
+
+Commit `2fee1e4` (2019-10-22, first in 4.7.2) added `var cache = { }` and query-result memoization. `parseCache` arrived still later (4.24.5, commit `1b999cb`).
+
+### 2. Direct code verification
+
+```
+$ grep -n "var cache =\|var parseCache =\|cache\[cacheKey\]" index.js
+(no output)
+```
+
+3.2.8 `index.js` resolves queries and returns `uniq(result)` with no result cache. `node.js` only has `filenessCache` / `configCache`, which the advisory says are unaffected.
+
+### 3. Advisory range is overly broad
+
+OSV lists 3.2.8 because the git event range is `introduced: 0`. The unbounded query cache does not exist in this tag.
+
+---
+
+## Timeline
+
+| Date | Event |
+|---|---|
+| 3.2.8 | No query-result cache in `index.js` |
+| 2019-10-22 | `2fee1e4` adds unbounded `cache` (4.7.2) |
+| 2025-01-08 | `1b999cb` adds `parseCache` (4.24.5) |
+| 2026-07-21 | `f2931a3` converts both to Maps capped at 500 |
+| 2026-08-11 | CVE-2026-73089 published as < 4.28.7 |
+
+---
+
+## Conclusion
+
+**CVE-2026-73089 is a false positive for browserslist@3.2.8.**
+
+No functional source patch is applicable. Scanner findings should be suppressed.
+
